# Recovery always runs permissive, whatever the installed ROM's boot cmdline says. The recovery boots with the
# ROM's kernel + header (installer / auto-reflash keep them); Infinity X has no androidboot.selinux=permissive, so
# init could not create the fscrypt keyring ("Failed to create keyring: Permission denied") and FBE decryption
# failed with "Unable to find device keyring". Only affects recovery mode; normal boot uses the ROM's own init.
import /init.recovery.wifi.rc
on early-init
    exec u:r:recovery:s0 root root -- /system/bin/setenforce 0
